		{
			description: [
				"The &eSmartwrench&r is RFTools' universal wrench - rotate, configure and disassemble any RFTools machine with one tool."
				""
				"&e&lTwo modes, switched by crouching:&r"
				"&7- &fNormal&7 - rotate and configure the block you click."
				"&7- &fSelect&7 - bind a machine to the wrench, then configure it from anywhere. This is how you set up a Matter Transmitter without walking back and forth across your island."
				""
				"&7It also picks machines up intact, keeping their inventory and settings - the same trick as Create's wrench. Never break an RFTools machine with a pickaxe.&r"
				""
				"&8Keep it in your hotbar for the whole chapter. Every block here expects it."
			]
			icon: "rftoolsbase:smartwrench"
			id: "115DC22612D3DD3F"
			rewards: [{
				id: "590102B397D47C7E"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Base"
			tasks: [{
				id: "1EB420483681C26B"
				item: "rftoolsbase:smartwrench"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bSmartwrench"
			x: -6.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"A &6Matter Transmitter&r paired with a &6Dialing Device&r teleports you between fixed points - point, dial, arrive."
				""
				"&e&lIt needs a Receiver at the far end and power at both.&r Once linked, the dialer remembers destinations, so a hub with one transmitter can reach every platform you have built."
				""
				"&7Cheaper and earlier than AE2 spatial or a Draconic teleporter, and it does not care how far apart the two ends are.&r"
			]
			icon: "rftoolsutility:matter_transmitter"
			id: "7B3DC7246B77DA93"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7F14583B9E2CEFC5"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Utility"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "4BCF4DD3E98887AF"
					item: "rftoolsutility:matter_transmitter"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "37915F214A0B819F"
					item: "rftoolsutility:dialing_device"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&bMatter Transmitters"
			x: -4.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"The &eBuilder&r reads a &eShape Card&r and executes it - quarry a cube, pump a lake, or clear an area, all without you lifting a pickaxe."
				""
				"&e&lThe Builder is the most versatile block in RFTools&r because the Shape Card decides what it does. Same machine, completely different jobs:"
				"&7- &fQuarry card&7 - mines everything in the defined region"
				"&7- &fVoid card&7 - mines and deletes, for clearing space"
				"&7- &fPump card&7 - drains fluids in the region"
				"&7- &fBuilder card&7 - &lplaces&r blocks from its inventory instead of removing them"
				"&7- &fFilter variants&7 - only ores, only non-ores, and so on"
				""
				"&e&lHow to aim it:&r right-click the card to open the shape editor, set dimensions and offsets, then preview with a &7Shape Card projector&r before you run it. The preview is the difference between quarrying a chunk and quarrying your base."
				""
				"&c&lIt is very power hungry&r, and silk-touch or fortune variants multiply that cost. Feed it from a Power Cell, not directly from a wind farm."
				""
				"&7On a void island the Builder shines as a &lconstruction&r tool as much as a mining one - filling platforms, clearing old builds, and shifting terrain in the dimensions you visit.&r"
			]
			icon: "rftoolsbuilder:builder"
			id: "6A03B5968E1CD99C"
			rewards: [{
				id: "508F308A8A4CC633"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Builder"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "64393341A21E157C"
					item: "rftoolsbuilder:builder"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "4314F4901BAD60A2"
					item: "rftoolsbuilder:shape_card_quarry"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&bThe Builder"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"RFTools' own power line, independent of everything else."
				""
				"&7- &fPower Cell&7 - stores RF at massive scale, and cells placed adjacent merge into one larger bank."
				"&7- &fBlazing Generator&7 - burns blaze rods to fill it."
				""
				"&e&lThe useful trick:&r Power Cells can be linked across dimensions with a Card, so power generated on your island is available on the Moon without running a single cable."
			]
			icon: "rftoolspower:cell1"
			id: "2E836BF44B65F66F"
			rewards: [{
				id: "54C901CAD4D7C37E"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Power"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "56F90F24029B3844"
					item: "rftoolspower:cell1"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "3237819C5422FAF2"
					item: "rftoolspower:blazing_generator"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&bPower Cells"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"The &eDimension Builder&r assembles &eDimlets&r into a custom pocket dimension - pick the biome, terrain and features, then step through."
				""
				"&e&lThis is RFTools' headline feature and the most powerful thing in the chapter.&r You are not visiting a dimension someone else designed - you are specifying one. Terrain type, biome, what blocks it is made of, whether it has mobs, whether it has a sky."
				""
				"&e&lThe workflow:&r"
				"&71.&r Collect &7Dimlets&r - each describes one property."
				"&72.&r Insert them into the &7Dimension Builder&r along with a Dimension Tab."
				"&73.&r Power it heavily while it builds. This costs a lot."
				"&74.&r Place the finished &7Dimension Cell&r in a &7Dimension Enscriber&r and step through the portal."
				""
				"&c&lThe dimension draws power continuously to stay alive.&r If your grid dies while you are inside, you are stranded until it comes back. Always carry a way out."
				""
				"&e&lWhy it matters on a skyblock:&r a custom dimension made entirely of one ore block is a genuinely unlimited resource supply. It is also, quite deliberately, expensive enough that you have to earn it."
				""
				"&8Start with a simple flat dimension to learn the system before spending your good dimlets."
			]
			icon: "rftoolsdim:dimension_builder"
			id: "5FF5138F14109D91"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7BF583322057371C"
				type: "xp_levels"
				xp_levels: 3
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Dimensions"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4A927B5EA3A53DB4"
				item: "rftoolsdim:dimension_builder"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bBuild Your Own Dimension"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"&eModular Storage&r stacks storage modules into a single controllable block, and the &eStorage Scanner&r finds any item across your whole base without opening a single chest."
				""
				"&e&lThe Storage Scanner is the part worth building.&r It indexes every inventory in a radius - chests, drawers, barrels, machine buffers - and gives you one searchable window across all of them. You can pull items out and push items back from that window."
				""
				"&e&lIt is not AE2, and that is the point.&r No cables, no channels, no controller, no power-hungry network. It reads chests you already have, exactly where they are. On a mid-game base that is often all you actually wanted."
				""
				"&7Set the scan radius carefully - a large radius over a big base costs performance every refresh. Tighten it to the room your storage actually occupies.&r"
				""
				"&e&lModular Storage&r itself is a single block whose capacity depends on the modules inside, remotely viewable from the Scanner. Useful, but the Scanner is the reason to be here."
				""
				"&8If you already have an ME network, the Scanner still earns its place - it sees the chests your AE2 system does not."
			]
			icon: "rftoolsstorage:modular_storage"
			id: "7CEFFFCF872943C8"
			rewards: [{
				id: "3BD8785ACF528B91"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Storage"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "285CB563C5D57DB8"
					item: "rftoolsstorage:modular_storage"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "39AB760E43BDFCDF"
					item: "rftoolsstorage:storage_scanner"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&bModular Storage"
			x: 6.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"The &6Programmer&r and &6Workbench&r let you build logic out of visual nodes instead of writing code."
				""
				"&e&lThis is the middle ground&r between redstone and ComputerCraft - more capable than a comparator chain, far less work than Lua. Drag nodes, wire them, drop the card into a Processor."
				""
				"&7Good for the jobs that are genuinely conditional: run this only when that tank is low, alarm if the reactor climbs, sort by NBT.&r"
			]
			icon: "rftoolscontrol:programmer"
			id: "6775474E8AE4DC25"
			rewards: [{
				id: "1CF1BC81C6CF9B0B"
				type: "xp_levels"
				xp_levels: 3
			}]
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "&7Control &8· suite mastered"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "6ED2EB3D58DA243F"
					item: "rftoolscontrol:programmer"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "7D3B00D3EEA17C93"
					item: "rftoolscontrol:workbench"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&bProgrammable Logic"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["68EF5F257321514B"]
			description: [
				"&eMachine Frames&r are the chassis of every RFTools machine, and the &eMachine Infuser&r upgrades them into &7Infused&r frames."
				""
				"&e&lInfused machines run faster and cheaper.&r The infuser consumes Dimensional Shards to upgrade a frame in place - worth doing for anything that runs constantly."
				""
				"&7RFTools is really seven separate mods sharing a frame: Base, Builder, Control, Dimensions, Power, Storage and Utility. Every one of them starts with this block.&r"
				""
				"&8Make a stack. You will build more RFTools machines than you expect."
			]
			icon: "rftoolsbase:machine_frame"
			id: "3F1C4431FD3C3253"
			rewards: [{
				id: "396D2476A39832AF"
