			title: "&bMachine Frames"
			x: -6.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6A03B5968E1CD99C"]
			description: [
				"A &eShape Card&r defines a region and an operation. The Builder just executes it."
				""
				"&e&lThe card types:&r"
				"&7- &fQuarry&7 - mine everything in the region"
				"&7- &fQuarry (silk / fortune)&7 - the same, with enchant behaviour"
				"&7- &fVoid&7 - mine and delete, for clearing"
				"&7- &fPump&7 - drain fluids"
				"&7- &fBuilder&7 - place blocks from inventory instead of removing"
				""
				"&c&lPreview before you run it.&r The shape editor renders a ghost of the affected region. This is the difference between quarrying a chunk and quarrying your base."
				""
				"&7Filters restrict the card to ores only, non-ores only, or a specific list. A filtered quarry card is far cheaper to run.&r"
			]
			icon: "rftoolsbuilder:builder"
			id: "1B7CF26A9E2A2A09"
			rewards: [{
				id: "37162A39CF1172C2"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Tell the Builder what to do"
			tasks: [{
				id: "48BCCC0C88A309A3"
				item: "rftoolsbuilder:builder"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bShape Cards"
			x: 0.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"A &eSpace Chamber&r captures a region of the world; the &eMover&r relocates it somewhere else."
				""
				"&e&lThis moves builds intact&r - machines, inventories, orientation and all. On a floating island where you inevitably outgrow your first platform, it is worth its cost the first time you use it."
				""
				"&7Define the chamber with corner blocks, scan it, then place the result. Large regions cost a great deal of power.&r"
				""
				"&8Create's Schematicannon rebuilds from materials; this genuinely teleports the original blocks."
			]
			icon: "rftoolsbuilder:space_chamber"
			id: "575506CCAB286D21"
			rewards: [{
				id: "496ED1BCF2C264B8"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Copy a whole build"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "2091A1C8BC244D5B"
					item: "rftoolsbuilder:space_chamber"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "7B8C2DC944B5E95C"
