				}
			]
			title: "&bSpace Chamber \\& Mover"
			x: 2.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6775474E8AE4DC25"]
			description: [
				"&eScreens&r display information from anywhere in your base - energy levels, machine status, item counts, time, player names."
				""
				"&e&lThey are modular.&r Each screen holds modules, and each module shows one thing. Add an Energy module pointed at your Induction Matrix, a Counter module on your ore output, a Clock, a Redstone indicator."
				""
				"&e&lA Screen Controller powers a whole wall of screens at once&r rather than wiring each one, and lets them read blocks far away."
				""
				"&7This is the cheapest monitoring in the pack - no computer, no Lua, no Advanced Peripherals. Just place and configure.&r"
			]
			icon: "rftoolsutility:screen"
			id: "12CE62FCAF4E41F9"
			rewards: [{
				id: "34CD58B22E160D56"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7A dashboard for your base"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "0CCF56E17B032021"
					item: "rftoolsutility:screen"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "2F0E79892ADEB0F8"
					item: "rftoolsutility:screen_controller"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&bScreens"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"&eRedstone Transmitters&r and &eReceivers&r carry a signal across any distance and between dimensions."
				""
				"&e&lPair them with a channel name&r and they behave as one wire. No repeaters, no dust, no chunk-loading the line between."
				""
				"&7Combined with a Sensor - which detects blocks, items, entities or growth in a region - you get remote automation triggers with no wiring at all.&r"
				""
				"&8The Counter, Timer and Sequencer blocks turn those signals into actual logic without a computer."
			]
			icon: "rftoolsutility:redstone_transmitter"
			id: "1A0B8EA199669395"
			rewards: [{
				id: "4CE5BA0C4F5E14DA"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Wireless signals"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "0068518E559A2A80"
					item: "rftoolsutility:redstone_transmitter"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "469F164F20295A68"
					item: "rftoolsutility:redstone_receiver"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&bRedstone Anywhere"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"RFTools' &eSequencer&r, &eTimer&r, &eCounter&r and logic gates replace sprawling redstone with single blocks."
				""
				"&e&lThe Sequencer is the standout&r - draw a 64-step pattern in its GUI and it emits that sequence on a clock. Machine timing, alternating outputs, pulse trains, all without a single repeater."
				""
				"&7The Timer is a clean adjustable clock. The Counter counts pulses and fires at a threshold. Between them you can build most factory control logic in three blocks.&r"
				""
				"&8Far easier to change later than a redstone build, and far kinder to server tick rate."
			]
			icon: "rftoolsutility:sequencer"
			id: "4735DC156D54E438"
			rewards: [{
				id: "5C2316E789077555"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Redstone without the dust"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7D4F6B5499D87EE4"
					item: "rftoolsutility:sequencer"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "440166ED1F2D784B"
					item: "rftoolsutility:timer"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&bLogic Blocks"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"The &eCrafter&r holds several recipes at once and crafts them from piped-in materials."
				""
				"&e&lThree tiers hold 2, 4 and 8 recipes.&r Unlike the Create Mechanical Crafter it needs no arrangement, and unlike AE2 autocrafting it needs no network - it just sits there making things."
				""
				"&e&lIt supports internal recipes&r, where the output of one recipe feeds the next inside the same machine. A single Crafter can turn ingots into a finished component through three steps."
				""
				"&7Good middle ground: cheaper than AE2, more flexible than a Create crafter array.&r"
			]
			icon: "rftoolsutility:crafter1"
			id: "7BAA210748EB9970"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2432BF4170D87DC8"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Recipe automation, tiered"
			tasks: [{
				id: "255A97D706CF6481"
				item: "rftoolsutility:crafter1"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bRFTools Crafter"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"The &eSpawner&r creates mobs from raw materials beamed in by &eMatter Beamers&r - no spawn eggs, no dark room, no spawner cage."
				""
				"&e&lThis is a real answer to a void world.&r Feed it the right materials and it produces the mob you specify, wherever you built it, regardless of light level or biome."
				""
				"&7Each mob needs specific matter types in specific amounts, shown in the spawner's GUI. Beamers deliver them from adjacent inventories.&r"
				""
				"&8Between this, Hostile Neural Networks and Ars Nouveau's Drygmy, a floating island has three completely different ways to farm mobs it cannot spawn."
			]
			icon: "rftoolsutility:spawner"
			id: "0BF501014A4D1EDE"
			rewards: [{
				id: "6748BC25D1515950"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Mobs from materials"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "2AC924666BB6B758"
					item: "rftoolsutility:spawner"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "28608FDFDEB840AC"
					item: "rftoolsutility:matter_beamer"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&bMatter Beamer \\& Spawner"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"The &eEnvironmental Controller&r applies potion effects to everything in a radius - or denies them."
				""
				"&e&lPermanent haste and night vision over your base&r is the obvious use, and it is very good. Feed it modules and power and it simply runs."
				""
				"&7It also has hostile-mob and player filters, so you can buff yourself while poisoning anything that wanders in.&r"
				""
				"&8Power draw scales with radius and module count. Keep the radius tight to your actual base."
			]
			icon: "rftoolsutility:environmental_controller"
			id: "62401BB46357F44D"
			rewards: [{
				id: "1AA4B5C84F405781"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Area effects on demand"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2EF609D895E4A619"
				item: "rftoolsutility:environmental_controller"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bEnvironmental Controller"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"A &eCharged Porter&r is a handheld teleporter - charge it, link it to a Matter Transmitter, and use it to jump there from anywhere."
				""
				"&e&lIt is the escape hatch.&r Deep in an Aether dungeon with a full inventory and low health, this gets you home without a rocket, a portal or a walk."
				""
				"&7It holds a charge and needs recharging between uses. The Advanced Charged Porter holds far more.&r"
				""
				"&8Pairs with the Matter Transmitters you already built at the start of this chapter."
			]
			icon: {
				Count: 1
				id: "rftoolsutility:charged_porter"
				tag: {
					Damage: 0
				}
			}
			id: "66C5190C6F47EDDF"
